---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const posts = (await getCollection('blog')).sort(
  (a, b) => new Date(b.data.pubDate).getTime() - new Date(a.data.pubDate).getTime()
);
---

<BaseLayout title="princefarming | Home">
  <div>
    <h2>Hello!</h2>  
    Princefarming = Michael Wynn
<p>Back in the late 90s when I was creating a hotmail account I was looking for an alias to go by, at the time it seemed like a neat/cool thing. I remember reading a Life Magazine article that had a picture of Prince Charles bent over looking at a garden, the caption was "Prince Farming". The rest is Internet History.
</p>
<p>If you came here looking for stuff about me and where I work etc. please see me on
</p>

<h2>Music</h2>
<p>
<a href="https://www.meltedwings.ca" target="_blank">Melted Wings</a> (my solo stuff)</p>

<a href="https://www.vickyvonvicky.com" target="_blank">Vicky von Vicky</a>
<br/>
  </div>
  <div class="feed">
    {posts.map((post) => (
      <article class="post-card">
        <header class="post-header">
          <h2>
            <a href={`/news/${post.id}`}>{post.data.title}</a>
          </h2>
          <div class="post-meta">
            <span>Posted on <time>{post.data.pubDate}</time></span>
          </div>
        </header>

        {post.data.image && (
          <a href={`/news/${post.id}`}>
            <img src={post.data.image} alt={post.data.title} class="featured-image" />
          </a>
        )}

        {post.data.description && (
          <p class="excerpt">{post.data.description}</p>
        )}

        <div class="post-footer">
          <a href={`/news/${post.id}`} class="read-more">Continue reading &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </article>
    ))}
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
